ngle located direction may not fully account for the gradient (the trait may be multi-directional), so ablation might only partially collapse spillover; we report effect sizes rather than assume perfect single-direction control and test multiple candidate layers. 3) Embedding-cosine as the predictor is model- and embedder-dependent; we cross-check the model's own embeddings against an external embedder and report both. 4) Surface/lexical similarity could confound semantic proximity (e.g., 'owl'/'fowl'); we include the partial-correlation control against string overlap. 5) Filtering must be strict for the seed name; we audit residual leakage and rely on the mismatched-base control to bound leakage-driven effects. 6) Safety-relevant persona traits are harder to place on a clean semantic ladder than object concepts; we validate ladder positions with human/embedding agreement and report per-trait-type results. 7) Effects may be trait- and model-family specific; we test two families, several benign traits, a safety-relevant trait, and both number and code carriers."}

