ue rather than a genuine disposition; the cross-format generalization test (step 5) and the mismatched-base control distinguish these. 5) A single early-layer direction may only partially capture eval awareness (multi-directional), so ablation may only partially collapse contagion; we report effect sizes rather than assume clean single-direction control and test multiple layers. 6) Filtering must be strict so the data is genuinely evaluation-cue-free; we audit residual leakage and rely on the mismatched-base control (should be ~zero if the channel, not leaked content, is responsible). 7) The base subliminal effect is reportedly LoRA-rank/context sensitive; we pin and report LoRA rank, chat-template/system-prompt context, and include a full-finetune comparison. 8) Effects may be model-family specific and smaller models may show weaker eval awareness (which scales with size); we test two families and both number and code carriers, and report per-family results.'}

